# Client-side routing: the app owns /waiting, /team/:slug and /access, but
# there is no file at those paths, so Netlify must hand every unmatched request
# to index.html and let React Router sort it out. 200, not 301 — the URL in the
# address bar has to stay where it is.
#
# Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so this lands at the site root.
# Real files (assets, fonts) are served before this rule is ever consulted.
/*    /index.html   200
